cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Double Torus — A Deterministic Quantum Simulation Kernel with Content-Addressed Verification"
abstract: >-
  The double-torus vortex algebra of the sequence 12487536901, with the Clay
  Millennium problems as proof of concept. Every claim recomputes from src/0.
  764 registered theorems, 758 of them carrying an executable proof. 37 Lean 4
  proof files compile in plain Lean with no Mathlib and no `sorry`; 101
  involution theorems and 49 registry rows are decided by the kernel with no
  axiom beyond propext and Quot.sound. What these files decide is the
  involution each Clay Millennium problem is stated across; what follows from
  that is stated by the author, under his name, and argued where such things
  are argued.

authors:
  - family-names: Rouschev
    given-names: Tsvetan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7312-9778"
